          {
            "id": "msg_tmp_w7jzoggbueh",
            "content": [
              {
                "annotations": [],
                "text": "An analysis of the training examples reveals the transformation rule:\n1. The grid is an $N \\times N$ square with odd dimension $N$, filled with a background color (7).\n2. The center of the grid is at coordinates $(c, c)$ where $c = (N - 1) / 2$.\n3. Each non-background pixel defines the color of a concentric square ring around the center based on its Chebyshev (L-infinity) distance from the center:\n   $$\\text{ring index } d = \\max(|r - c|, |k - c|)$$\n4. The output grid consists of concentric square borders around the center $(c, c)$, where each cell at Chebyshev distance $d$ from the center is filled with the color found at distance $d$ in the input.\n\nI am ready for the test input.",
